1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,581
Day 56: mini-swe-agent, a coding agent of about a hundred

2
00:00:04,581 --> 00:00:05,063
lines.

3
00:00:05,063 --> 00:00:09,323
We asked local models to fix one bug in our own repo.

4
00:00:09,773 --> 00:00:12,046
It comes from the SWE-bench team.

5
00:00:12,046 --> 00:00:16,247
Its only tool is bash, and the agent class is about a hundred

6
00:00:16,247 --> 00:00:17,900
and fifty lines of code.

7
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:20,918
The model replies with a bash command,

8
00:00:20,918 --> 00:00:24,770
and the agent appends every output to one linear history.

9
00:00:25,220 --> 00:00:29,034
Each command runs in a fresh shell inside a container without

10
00:00:29,034 --> 00:00:32,035
network, until the model echoes a submit marker.

11
00:00:32,485 --> 00:00:35,677
Only gemma4 fixed it, four times out of six.

12
00:00:35,677 --> 00:00:37,273
Qwen models never did.

13
00:00:37,273 --> 00:00:41,263
A sed command without escaped brackets silently changed

14
00:00:41,263 --> 00:00:44,165
nothing, and five runs submitted anyway.

15
00:00:44,615 --> 00:00:45,486
MIT licensed.

16
00:00:45,486 --> 00:00:49,370
Source, license and the full logs are linked on GitHub and

17
00:00:49,370 --> 00:00:50,710
in the Zenn article.
